                        "form": "бала́нде"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "03bbfec9-0fbd-40f6-8eb8-eaac9f0ecf6f",
                        "entry_id": "eefe701c-9c94-3d9d-83ba-3775f5be13ef",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "бала́ндах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "31e4dc6f-24c6-3dcc-b9b5-81c9470060b7",
                        "entry_id": "eefe701c-9c94-3d9d-83ba-3775f5be13ef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "прост. очень жидкая, обычно невкусная похлёбка"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "993bc209-fa3d-4277-abec-0f79a717b9c8",
                                "sense_id": "31e4dc6f-24c6-3dcc-b9b5-81c9470060b7",
                                "text": "Уже ни хлеба, ни каши, ни баланды не принимало его тело, обречённое распасться."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a07b873-e14d-4536-b9f5-b7736b1a3de3",
                                "sense_id": "31e4dc6f-24c6-3dcc-b9b5-81c9470060b7",
                                "text": "Каждое утро в карцере получаешь четверть литра кипятка и трёхсотграммовую пайку, а раз в три дня, в обед, — половник самой жидкой баланды."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0fc1c10b-6daa-3f14-9258-a3308d890673",
                        "entry_id": "eefe701c-9c94-3d9d-83ba-3775f5be13ef",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., прост. пустой разговор, ненужная или лживая болтовня"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5f65a019-fe6a-45dc-a89d-de165f1b7067",
                                "sense_id": "0fc1c10b-6daa-3f14-9258-a3308d890673",
                                "text": "Тунгусов плёл путаную, замысловатую баланду, всаживая в неё имена знакомых балерин, знаменитого Лоуренса, описания дворцов, события из жизни трех мушкетёров, плавание жюль-верновского Наутилуса."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "324e20f3-5961-4af5-80bb-f4c2d17dca7c",
                        "source_entry_id": "eefe701c-9c94-3d9d-83ba-3775f5be13ef",
                        "source_sense_description": "жидкая похлёбка",
                        "target_lang_word": "skilly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "skilly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "41aa7b21-d1a5-34aa-bfbb-1130e40eb26e",
                                        "entry_id": "186cfd7b-03ec-358b-9b57-2bdb1ef79770",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Skillygalee."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0808a724-4fcc-4c14-b148-92f0126d78a3",
                                                "sense_id": "41aa7b21-d1a5-34aa-bfbb-1130e40eb26e",
                                                "text": "“I would be given for supper six ounces of bread and ‘three parts of skilly.’ ‘Three parts’ means three-quarters of a pint, and ‘skilly’ is a fluid concoction of three quarts of oatmeal stirred into three buckets and a half of hot water.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "028bad1e-5a30-4c10-b4d8-5160a927b69c",
                                                "sense_id": "41aa7b21-d1a5-34aa-bfbb-1130e40eb26e",
                                                "text": "Of course unlike the officers we never got fresh bread, we got what came from barrels stored in the lower peak and under the steward's padlock. Pantiles baked brick hard, mouldy oats for skilly, dried peas for soup, embalmed pork and beef more fat and bone than meat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "skilly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53e60755-7266-3097-b880-5f77af12a03a",
                                        "entry_id": "d5279a21-584c-3a63-a038-b4f300fb3451",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Skilled, skilful."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Northern-England",
                                            "Scotland"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "517560fd-c7ac-47fc-b0a3-1d304ed4c4a3",
                                                "sense_id": "53e60755-7266-3097-b880-5f77af12a03a",
                                                "text": "So, being a fell impatient man, and skilly with his hands, he took Sam Gourlay a clout in the lug that couped him down in the stour […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
